WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:01.967
-Last time we talked,

00:00:01.967 --> 00:00:03.235
and I think it finally
actually happened.

00:00:03.235 --> 00:00:04.371
-It did.
-It did.

00:00:04.371 --> 00:00:05.971
-Yeah.
-You had Rihanna on the show.

00:00:05.971 --> 00:00:07.106
-I did.
-Wow!

00:00:07.106 --> 00:00:08.441
-Yeah.
-What was it like?

00:00:08.441 --> 00:00:11.978
-It was the dream, yeah.
It was beyond my wildest dreams.

00:00:11.978 --> 00:00:15.215
We went day drinking, which is
something we do on the show.

00:00:15.215 --> 00:00:16.716
[ Laughter ]

00:00:16.716 --> 00:00:18.151
-I can't believe
she said yes to that.

00:00:18.151 --> 00:00:20.252
-I know!
[ Laughter ]

00:00:20.252 --> 00:00:22.322
Why would you say yes to that?
-Why would you say yes to that?

00:00:22.322 --> 00:00:23.756
-But it was amazing.
People say,

00:00:23.756 --> 00:00:25.525
"What's it like
drinking with Rihanna?"

00:00:25.525 --> 00:00:27.660
You know, like,
there's some people, like,

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:29.295
the more you drink
over the course of the night,

00:00:29.295 --> 00:00:31.130
the more they start
looking like Rihanna?

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:32.298
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:32.298 --> 00:00:34.434
-Like, imagine starting there.
-Wow!

00:00:34.434 --> 00:00:35.602
[ Laughter ]
Wow.

00:00:35.602 --> 00:00:37.103
-You know what I mean?
-Yeah. Oh, my gosh.

00:00:37.103 --> 00:00:39.105
Must be amazing.
-But she was so much fun.

00:00:39.105 --> 00:00:42.041
And she's the nicest person
in the world, and it was --

00:00:42.041 --> 00:00:44.810
it was a blast.
-But what do you do after a --

00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:46.546
Like, when does day drinking
end for you?

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:48.681
-So, it ends -- unfortunately,
because, it's day drinking,

00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:50.950
it ends in the afternoon,
and then I go home

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:53.553
to a wife and children.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:53.553 --> 00:00:56.356
And it's never ended where
we haven't had some --

00:00:56.356 --> 00:00:58.757
like, where I've gotten
a little snitty with my wife.

00:00:58.757 --> 00:01:01.694
Because, like, I'll come home
and knock over a lamp,

00:01:01.694 --> 00:01:03.395
and she'll roll her eyes,
as you would,

00:01:03.395 --> 00:01:05.698
when your husband comes
home at 4:30 super trashed.

00:01:05.698 --> 00:01:07.033
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:08.133
-And she'll just go, "Ugh!"

00:01:08.133 --> 00:01:10.003
And then I'll say,
"It's for work!"

00:01:10.003 --> 00:01:11.470
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:13.606
"I was --
I was working with Rihanna!"

00:01:13.606 --> 00:01:16.442
-"This is for work!
I put food on the table."

00:01:16.442 --> 00:01:18.244
-"I drank to pay for that lamp!"

00:01:18.244 --> 00:01:20.146
[ Laughter ]

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:21.981
-Makes no sense.

00:01:21.981 --> 00:01:23.549
I have a picture
your wife sent to us.

00:01:23.549 --> 00:01:24.684
-Yeah.
-She wanted to show us

00:01:24.684 --> 00:01:26.252
what you look like
after day drinking.

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:27.954
-Yeah.
That's me in the --

00:01:27.954 --> 00:01:29.154
-This is you in the hallway.

00:01:29.154 --> 00:01:30.155
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:30.155 --> 00:01:31.290
You took a nap?

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:32.958
-I took a full nap
in the hallway.

00:01:32.958 --> 00:01:36.462
That's my --
-You took a nap in your hallway.

00:01:36.462 --> 00:01:39.699
-That is the most --
My mother-in-law took that.

00:01:39.699 --> 00:01:41.835
And, also, this is the most
mother-in-law thing.

00:01:41.835 --> 00:01:43.570
She put a water down next to me.

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:45.004
[ Laughter ]

00:01:45.004 --> 00:01:47.740
-"Stay hydrated."
-Yeah, stay hydrated.

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:49.642
-But you told me
there's one thing --

00:01:49.642 --> 00:01:51.310
'Cause I said,
"Is she just perfect?

00:01:51.310 --> 00:01:52.511
Is Rihanna just awesome?"
-Yeah.

00:01:52.511 --> 00:01:54.781
-Like, "Yes,
she's everything, perfect."

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:56.849
I said, "Is there one thing
that she doesn't do well?"

00:01:56.849 --> 00:01:58.118
And you go,
"There might be one thing."

00:01:58.118 --> 00:02:00.453
-Yeah, she, at one point,
took my phone

00:02:00.453 --> 00:02:04.357
and took a bunch of pictures
while we were day drinking.

00:02:04.357 --> 00:02:05.925
And then, when I went through
them and looked at them,

00:02:05.925 --> 00:02:08.061
I'm like, "Rihanna's bad
at taking pictures."

00:02:08.061 --> 00:02:09.229
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.229 --> 00:02:11.263
-See, I disagree.
I think this is a great picture.

00:02:11.263 --> 00:02:12.264
-I think
that's not a good picture.

00:02:12.264 --> 00:02:14.367
-I would --
[ Laughter ]

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:15.768
-I think that's poorly framed.

00:02:15.768 --> 00:02:17.970
-I would post that on Instagram.
-I think that's got a bad --

00:02:17.970 --> 00:02:19.506
And I don't think --
Well, that's a good one.

00:02:19.506 --> 00:02:20.639
This is a good picture of us.
It is.

00:02:20.639 --> 00:02:23.543
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:23.543 --> 00:02:25.378
-Yeah.
-That's a memory right there.

00:02:25.378 --> 00:02:27.346
-Yeah, that's --
I think that's actually called

00:02:27.346 --> 00:02:29.382
the Rihanna filter.
-Yeah, it is, yeah.

00:02:29.382 --> 00:02:30.883
[ Laughter ]
Is that really?

00:02:30.883 --> 00:02:32.352
-Yeah, they just put
Rihanna in a picture,

00:02:32.352 --> 00:02:33.686
and then you look happy.
-She's not even there.

00:02:33.686 --> 00:02:35.521
Yeah.
Are you guys, like, buddies now?

00:02:35.521 --> 00:02:37.090
Do you have each other's --
-No.

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:39.492
[ Laughter ]
I mean, I think highly of her.

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:40.760
I think we're friendly,
like, and whatnot.

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:41.894
-You don't have
her cellphone number?

00:02:41.894 --> 00:02:43.896
-I wouldn't want it.
-No.

00:02:43.896 --> 00:02:45.931
-I think it would be, like,
too dangerous to have.

00:02:45.931 --> 00:02:47.466
[ Laughter ]
Like, you know what I mean?

00:02:47.466 --> 00:02:49.269
Like, I would like spend
all day thinking, like,

00:02:49.269 --> 00:02:50.736
"What's a funny thing
to text Rihanna?"

00:02:50.736 --> 00:02:51.770
I think that --
[ Laughter ]

00:02:51.770 --> 00:02:53.105
-Yeah, it would just be
too much.

00:02:53.105 --> 00:02:54.606
You already have a job.
-Yeah, I already have a job.

00:02:54.606 --> 00:02:56.275
I feel like certain things --
like, I shouldn't have

00:02:56.275 --> 00:02:58.278
Rihanna's phone number
in the same way

00:02:58.278 --> 00:03:00.012
Trump shouldn't
have nuclear codes.

00:03:00.012 --> 00:03:02.615
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:02.615 --> 00:03:04.850
-Someone near us can have them.
-Someone near us can have them,

00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:06.418
but you shouldn't have them.
-No, no, no.

00:03:06.418 --> 00:03:09.688
-Speaking of Trump,
the impeachment hearings

00:03:09.688 --> 00:03:11.757
are going on all this week.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:11.757 --> 00:03:14.260
-Any surprises?
What do you have to expect?

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:16.262
-I mean, it's --
I mean, it's weird because

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:17.930
we kind of know what
everybody's gonna say,

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:19.698
but it's still fascinating
to watch the words

00:03:19.698 --> 00:03:21.867
come out of their mouths
as opposed to, you know,

00:03:21.867 --> 00:03:25.405
reading, you know, what they
said in closed testimony.

00:03:25.405 --> 00:03:26.905
But, you know,
I've gotten so bad --

00:03:26.905 --> 00:03:28.707
I know now
that I can't predict anything.

00:03:28.707 --> 00:03:30.810
I've been wrong
about everything for so long.

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:32.311
-Really?
-So you just kind of, like,

00:03:32.311 --> 00:03:34.480
just, like, you know, buckle in
and watch the ride.

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:35.748
-With this administration?

00:03:35.748 --> 00:03:37.216
-Yeah, just with
the news these days.

00:03:37.216 --> 00:03:38.518
Like, nothing --
it feels like --

00:03:38.518 --> 00:03:39.819
-How?
Like, "This is happening."

00:03:39.819 --> 00:03:41.320
-Yeah.
-"Okay, we're doing this now.

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:42.755
All right."
-And, I mean, the testimony

00:03:42.755 --> 00:03:46.024
is fascinating, 'cause, you
know, one side asks questions,

00:03:46.024 --> 00:03:47.727
and people say things,
and you go, "Oh, that's bad,"

00:03:47.727 --> 00:03:48.927
and then you watch
the other side being like,

00:03:48.927 --> 00:03:50.296
"But, I mean, was it that bad?"

00:03:50.296 --> 00:03:51.431
And you're like,
"Yeah, no, it was."

00:03:51.431 --> 00:03:52.664
[ Laughter ]

00:03:52.664 --> 00:03:54.100
But that's like
their only defense right now.

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:55.734
It's like, "But, seriously,
there's worse things, right?"

00:03:55.734 --> 00:03:56.903
And you're like, "I don't know.

00:03:56.903 --> 00:03:58.237
I guess so,
but I don't know what it is."

00:03:58.237 --> 00:03:59.238
-"Why are we --"
Yeah, it's unbelievable.

00:03:59.238 --> 00:04:00.706
-Yeah.
-Do you have news on

00:04:00.706 --> 00:04:02.909
in your house, like,
around your wife and kids?

00:04:02.909 --> 00:04:04.544
-My kids are total news junkies.
3 and 1.

00:04:04.544 --> 00:04:06.012
-They really are?
-Yeah.

00:04:06.012 --> 00:04:09.215
The problem is one of them --
The 3-year-old loves MSNBC...

00:04:09.215 --> 00:04:11.550
[ Laughter ]
...1-year-old loves Fox News.

00:04:11.550 --> 00:04:12.618
-Fox News.
-Yeah.

00:04:12.618 --> 00:04:13.652
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, that's tough.

00:04:13.652 --> 00:04:15.355
That's tough.
-They're cartoonier,

00:04:15.355 --> 00:04:16.789
so he likes that.
Yeah.

00:04:16.789 --> 00:04:18.358
-They're different humans.
-They're just different people,

00:04:18.358 --> 00:04:19.425
so we have to get them
different TV.

00:04:19.425 --> 00:04:20.926
-But the baby --
So, 3 already?

00:04:20.926 --> 00:04:23.095
-3 1/2 and 1 1/2, yeah.
-Oh, my gosh.

00:04:23.095 --> 00:04:25.464
-It's really fun.
They're just --

00:04:25.464 --> 00:04:27.600
They're good dudes, and they
like hanging out together.

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:29.969
-Yeah.
-The other -- we have these --

00:04:29.969 --> 00:04:31.670
They have a pair
of noise-canceling headphones

00:04:31.670 --> 00:04:32.772
for babies.
-Yeah.

00:04:32.772 --> 00:04:34.039
-And the 3-year-old
likes to wear them

00:04:34.039 --> 00:04:36.009
'cause he likes to pretend
he's a helicopter pilot.

00:04:36.009 --> 00:04:38.177
And the 1-year-old
likes to wear them

00:04:38.177 --> 00:04:39.912
just to wear them
and walk around.

00:04:39.912 --> 00:04:41.647
But they're noise-canceling,
so you can't hear.

00:04:41.647 --> 00:04:42.949
So the other day,
the 3-year-old said,

00:04:42.949 --> 00:04:44.349
"I want those."
And I was like,

00:04:44.349 --> 00:04:46.152
"You have to ask your brother
if you can have them."

00:04:46.152 --> 00:04:47.820
So he walks over to the
1-year-old, and he says,

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:49.889
"Can I have those?"
But they're noise-canceling.

00:04:49.889 --> 00:04:52.625
So they just look at each other
for 10 seconds.

00:04:52.625 --> 00:04:57.096
[ Laughter ]

00:04:57.096 --> 00:04:59.298
And then, the 3-year-old
looks at me and goes,

00:04:59.298 --> 00:05:01.533
"He said yes."
[ Laughter ]

00:05:01.533 --> 00:05:02.901
-Thataboy!
-There you go!

00:05:02.901 --> 00:05:04.370
-Thataboy right there!
-Punch line!

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:06.372
-That's a smart kid.

